; Override an ambient NODE_ENV=production so `npm install` always installs
; devDependencies.  Background agents and some shell setups inherit
; NODE_ENV=production, which makes npm silently skip devDependencies — the
; project then fails to build (no vite, no tailwind, no @xterm) with no
; warning.  Pinning here keeps `npm install` deterministic regardless of
; the surrounding environment.
;
; npm 11+ form — the older `production=false` key works but emits a
; deprecation warning telling you to use `--omit=dev` (which is the
; opposite direction).  `include=dev` is the right modern key.
include=dev
